    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, our lineup leans heavily into aggressive base-running matchups and advantageous pitching environments to maximize our 5x5 output. **Seiya Suzuki** (73.90) headlines our offensive attack; he benefits from an elite combination of a favorable hitter\u2019s park, favorable wind conditions, and a strong platoon advantage against the lefty Abbott, allowing him to easily clear our elite threshold. Following closely are **Corbin Carroll** (71.00) and **Brice Turang** (70.37). **Brice Turang** remains a core tactical play, as he faces a pitcher with a slow delivery, providing the green light we need to pursue stolen bases\u2014our scarcest and most prioritized category. **Jose Caballero** (66.99) also earns a strong start, with a substantial 13% boost from his platoon edge against the lefty Bennett, while **Josh Naylor** (66.82) offers high-floor production batting in the heart of the order against the hittable Soriano.\n\nThe most difficult decision on our bench was leaving **Vinnie Pasquantino** (47.21) out of the utility slot. While he historically provides reliable production, a negative platoon adjustment against the lefty Foster Griffin suppressed his efficiency score below the utility start threshold occupied by **Isaac Paredes** (54.07), who remains in the lineup due to a superior platoon outlook against Nolan McLean. We are proceeding with caution regarding **Gabriel Moreno**, whose start remains subject to final lineup confirmation; however, if he slots into the #3 hole as projected, the wind-aided park factors make him a viable, if marginal, start. With **James Wood** still sidelined on the IL, we continue to rely on the depth of our outfield corps\u2014specifically **Henry Bolte** (60.56)\u2014to bridge the gap, despite a minor platoon tax against the right-handed Shane Baz. We will monitor all \"Lineup Pending\" designations closely, as any shuffle affecting **Brice Turang** or **Corbin Carroll** could necessitate a pivot to ensure we are not leaving potential stolen bases on the table.",
